// The cards. A card is [title, line]; a strategy card is [sentence, author or ""].
const DECKS = {};

DECKS.stance = {name:"Stance", hint:"Who you are while you make it", cards:[
["The Forest-Goer","Lives in the world but doesn't play its game. Discreet, curious, never on television."],
["The Skimmer","Quietly tries to end up with a little more than everyone else."],
["The Monitor","Warned his superiors. Nobody listened. Now he watches the disaster arrive, on schedule."],
["The Crust","Slippers, a book, silence. Asks nothing more of the evening."],
["The Over-Empath","Tunes to everyone's wavelength to avoid a quarrel, until there is no one left inside."],
["The Mythomaniac","Exists only as long as someone pretends to believe him."],
["The Wrecker in Passing","Breaks things on the way through, drunk on speed: \"I'm already gone.\""],
["The Dimwit Rebel","Defies authority loudly, then is furious when authority won't negotiate."],
["The Turncoat","Changes sides, and with them, destiny."],
["The Absurd Prince","Has found his axis, however tiny: partridge hunting, horror films, the 10K run."],
["The Observer","Watches and takes notes. Always slightly to one side."],
["The Careless Amateur","Succeeds without effort, in front of the specialist who has worked all his life."],
["The Motivation Faker","Wears the corporate mask with real dedication."],
["She Who Wants to Be Published","Gets there at fifty, and feels nothing at all."],
["The Fallow Composer","For him, music has become definitively incongruous."],
["The Love Tracker","Never lives his love; he scans each gesture until the scanned one slips."],
["The Heir Collector","Inherits an older collector's album, and loses all desire."],
["The One Who Stays","Everyone leaves. He stays planted there."],
["The Believer in Signs","Reads every coincidence as a message from the universe."],
["The Forty-Year-Old Don Juan","Installs a \"possible mother\" in his flat, and finds he can no longer love at all."],
["The Old Rebel","Tells you about his defeats, one by one, with a kind of pride."],
["The Symmetric Rebel","Black instead of pink, night instead of sunset: the exact reverse of what he hates."],
["The Spectacle Idiot","\"When a society reaches saturation, all that's left is to appear.\""],
["The Lover of Words","Lives entirely through sentences, a little to the side of things."],
["The Velleitary Artist","Wants to be an artist, has nothing to say, and suffers for it daily."],
["The Magellan","Leaves a terrible life for another one, and discovers the Pacific is even bigger."],
["The Pessimism Teacher","Helps people live by telling them life has no meaning."],
["The Ordinary Zelig","Becomes whoever he's standing next to."],
["The Ultrasolution Gunner","At parties, fires his solution to your problem before you've finished explaining it."],
["The Sullen Bus Driver","One day parks the bus sideways, lets everyone off, and walks home to the sound of horns."],
["The Exhausted Switchboard Girl","Her phone never stops. On the bridge, she says: \"Listen carefully, my love…\""],
["The Gothic Boy","Fascinated by death until the day he gets a real illness."],
["The Old Man Called Al","Pours a whisky, reads ten pages, and waits while the shouting idiots crash into the tree."],
["The Woman Who Sees Signs","Then the signs start agreeing with each other."],
["The Pink-Wig Hostess","A sociology student, studying how mankind is heading for its doom."],
["The Grandfather on the Phone","Calls from a phone box and plays the monster, to cure the boy who always picks up."],
["The Collector Who Never Read","A box of uncut books on Napoleon, kept for forty years."],
["The Courtier of \"It's Deliberate\"","Dresses up every failure as a strategy, until he believes it."],
["The Man Who Plays Dumb","It began as a joke. Now it's simpler."],
["The Type Who Knew Everyone","And whom nobody knows."],
["The Napoleon Expert","Meets the woman who knows everything about Joan of Arc."],
["The Lazy Sensualist","Moves slowly through a team of people in a hurry."],
["The Well-Dressed Prophet","And his polite listener, who keeps nodding."],
["The Man of the Second-Rate Life","Not unhappy. Just second-rate, and aware of it."],
["The Shy Candyfloss Seller","Gentle, kind, and very tired."],
["The Gothic Father","Strips the nursery wallpaper whistling a song about death."],
["The Musician Who Loses Her Kingdom","A star in her field; outside it, she falls apart."],
["The Overworked Husband","Works until his unconscious finds a way to say \"enough\": the crash, the infarct."],
["The Retired Western Fan","Makes lists. Endless, perfect lists."],
["The Girl Who Is \"Too Eager\"","\"I'm too eager to be later, for happiness.\""],
["The Polar Longing Man","Wants to go back, forever, to dark and cold places."],
["The Sentinel","Night watch in the trenches, 1916. Someone is watching him too."]]};

DECKS.form = {name:"Form", hint:"The shape the work wants", cards:[
["Fracture it.","Cut it into many sections with sudden jumps. Keep one logic underneath."],
["Make it one long rise.","From the first moment to the last, it only grows."],
["Turn it into a journey.","No return to the start. Each part goes somewhere new."],
["Make it a place.","Stop advancing. Let it be a room the audience stays in."],
["Let it swell.","Take something still and inflate it slowly until it fills everything."],
["State it, then mutate it.","Say the idea once, then let it change without ever coming back."],
["Bring it back altered.","Repeat a part, but never the same way twice."],
["Weld three things.","Take three unrelated pieces and join them. Add echoes between them."],
["Wind it like a spring.","Build tension, release, build tighter, release bigger."],
["Put everything in the passage.","Make the transition the best part, not the arrival."],
["Make a triptych.","Three panels, three moments, one tiny story."],
["Classify it.","Organise it as a typology: kinds, examples, exceptions."],
["Make a list.","Only a list of things, reasons or moments. Nothing else."],
["Timestamp it.","Organise it hour by hour, like a diary of one day."],
["Start with one gear.","Add a part at a time until the machine fills the hall."],
["Funnel it.","Begin with the biggest question, end with the smallest practical detail."],
["Make a refrain.","One part returns five times, changed each time."],
["Split the screen.","Show two things happening at once, side by side."],
["Escalate.","Each example more extreme than the last, then a comic drop."],
["Do twelve variations.","One simple theme, twelve treatments."],
["Follow a walk.","Go at walking pace and use what you pass on the way."],
["Do it in one breath.","No pause from beginning to end."],
["Cut out the transitions.","Only moments, separated by space."],
["Hide an engine.","Simple surface, complex mechanism underneath."],
["Pile up small oddities.","Keep a perfectly normal frame and fill it with tiny strange details."]]};

DECKS.move = {name:"Move", hint:"What to do", cards:[
["Take something away.","Remove one element and never put it back."],
["Hold one thing still.","Freeze one element and change everything beneath it."],
["Choose a pivot.","Pick one fixed point. Make everything else turn around it."],
["Knock one part out of step.","In a tidy whole, let one element drift off the rhythm."],
["Add small creatures.","Add tiny elements that do their own thing, ignoring the main event."],
["Bring the foundation in late.","Let the base arrive later than expected and wander before it settles."],
["Decide every detail.","Don't let anything fall where it happens to. Choose each one."],
["Stretch the extremes.","Make wide leaps in a very short space."],
["Start too quiet.","So small or faint that people lean in. Then grow."],
["Break it, then go higher.","Build, shatter, restart one step above."],
["Make one brutal shift.","A single sudden change of key, colour or tone."],
["Shift step by step.","Change register gradually, one notch at a time."],
["Approach, don't arrive.","Get close to the obvious resolution three times. Never go there."],
["Let one element escape.","One part steps outside the frame. Does the rest follow?"],
["Open, then close.","Keep it tight, open wide for a moment, tighten again."],
["Sharpen the centre, blur the edges.","Hard and precise in the middle, soft all around."],
["Bring it close.","Remove all distance. Close to the eye, the ear, the skin."],
["Push it far away.","Distance everything until it becomes a dream."],
["Remove the seam.","Blend two parts so no one can tell where one ends."],
["Add a quiet passage.","A stretch that refuses to show off."],
["Make one deliberate mistake.","Exactly one wrong thing, placed on purpose."],
["Fill the silences.","Put the main voice into the gaps of the background."],
["Change the pulse.","Halfway, switch the underlying rhythm without warning."],
["Mix too many textures.","So many that the work can't be pigeonholed."],
["Promote the background.","What usually accompanies becomes the main line."],
["Swap the roles.","Every element does another element's job."],
["Stack it into a wall.","Pile up the same element until it becomes architecture."],
["Vary one motif obsessively.","One phrase, one shape, one colour, varied ten times."],
["Bury your best idea.","Let it appear for a second, half-hidden. Never state it in full."],
["Kick it forward.","Every time it could settle, relaunch it."],
["Refuse to develop.","Stay in place, like an object turning slowly."],
["Pair it with something.","Make it to be experienced with one specific picture, sound or place."],
["Let it slip.","Nothing changes abruptly; shift everything a little."],
["Offer three explanations.","Each one cancels the previous."],
["Give it a personality.","Treat the machine as an animal, the object as a person."],
["Stare until it's strange.","Look at an ordinary element until it becomes odd. Use that."],
["Contradict the mood.","Make the setting go against the emotion."],
["Add the opposite.","Give every element its exact contrary somewhere."],
["Show it three times.","The same moment from three positions."],
["Group unlike things.","Put together things that look very different."],
["Add one cold detail.","A flat, precise, unflattering detail in the middle of beauty."],
["Add one laconic detail.","A small thing with very long reach."],
["Spoil the perfect moment.","Make it perfect, then let something from outside ruin it."],
["Choose the sensible option.","Where the genre wants passion, choose prudence."],
["Reverse the cliché.","Take the expected scenario and do the reasonable thing instead."],
["Hide the engine.","Make the most important part invisible, but felt."],
["Look through something.","A window, a fence, a curtain, a filter."],
["Give the silent thing a voice.","Write its inner monologue."],
["Write the title first.","Name the finished work, then make what the name promises."],
["Keep the accident.","The slip, the blur, the wrong take: keep it if it says something."],
["Add more ideas, tighten the form.","More ideas than feels safe, held by a stricter structure."]]};

DECKS.twist = {name:"Twist", hint:"What drifts", cards:[
["Make one detail wrong.","Everything realistic, except one discreet thing."],
["Remove a shadow.","One thing lacks what everything else has."],
["Reverse the roles.","The horse rides the man. The tool uses the hand."],
["Make one thing look back.","Everything ignores the audience; one element stares straight at it."],
["Make it ambiguous.","Is it a fight or a game? Let both readings work."],
["Put someone on the roof.","In the middle of the drama, a small figure doing something unexplained."],
["Hide what they're looking at.","Everyone faces something we never see."],
["Give them the wrong worry.","Faced with danger, what bothers them is a trivial detail."],
["Break the scale.","Make the huge thing tiny, or the tiny thing huge."],
["Change the season.","Spring in December, snow in July."],
["Freeze one thing.","One living thing perfectly still among moving ones."],
["Run it backwards.","Make it in reverse and present it forwards."],
["Oversize the engine.","One part far too powerful for the rest."],
["Plant an omen.","A harmless detail just before the turn, announcing it."],
["Let something wild in.","An untamed element enters the circle of light."],
["Make the fun sound forced.","Everyone is enjoying it. It rings slightly false."],
["Swap audience and actors.","The watchers perform; the performers watch."],
["Hide the emotion inside.","A feeling we can only guess."],
["Hang it by a thread.","Something heavy held up by almost nothing."],
["Put depth below.","Under the calm surface, a vertiginous mass."],
["Add an eye.","One gaze with more eyes than it should have."],
["Add a presence behind.","Something unseen at their back. Then the ground cracks."],
["Make the goal vanish.","It disappears the moment it is reached."],
["Let someone declare it sublime.","Ordinary, until an authority says otherwise."],
["Let the mask slip.","For one second, the professional face falls off."],
["Make it happen three times.","The same thing turns up from three directions."],
["Give too much.","So much of what you love that desire goes out."],
["Plant a lure.","Something attractive, placed there to deceive."],
["Make it pay now, cost later.","The benefit is immediate; the price comes at the end."],
["Make every exit worse.","Both options are wrong, and the escape is too."],
["Make two feelings collide.","Two extreme opposite emotions, at the same time."],
["Turn the danger into luck.","What looked like a threat is a windfall."],
["Hide a second danger.","React to the threat, then reveal a worse one behind it."],
["Let it arrive sideways.","What you feared comes, but obliquely."],
["Keep the ceremony going.","It's over; the rituals carry on."],
["Deliver a message late.","Something arrives in the wrong place, years later."]]};

DECKS.constraint = {name:"Constraint", hint:"The rule you take on", cards:[
["One hour.","Start now. Finish within sixty minutes."],
["Same format every time.","Same size, same length, same frame."],
["One colour.","A single dominant colour, tone or ingredient."],
["No retouching.","Keep the first pass."],
["No ornaments.","No adjectives, no decoration. Nouns and verbs only, in any medium."],
["Here and now.","Only what is within reach today."],
["Three-quarters strength.","Go fast and give less than everything."],
["A refrain.","One element returns at every stage, unchanged."],
["Twelve answers.","Twelve different responses to the same starting point."],
["Explain it to a child first.","Then make it."],
["Stop dead.","End in the middle of a gesture."],
["One tiny subject.","About something minuscule, and nothing else."],
["Fragments only.","No transitions. Let them jump."],
["Date every part.","Each part stamped with a time and the weather."],
["Toys only.","No living things. Objects play every role."],
["Nothing bigger than a coin.","Work at macro scale."],
["Two planes.","The observed in front, the observer behind."],
["Pair it.","Put it next to an unrelated thing and let them talk."],
["True, but not a document.","It must look real and must not be a record."],
["Make it missable.","The twist must go unnoticed at first glance."],
["Start from the bottom layer.","Every decision follows the lowest element."],
["Closer.","Halve every distance."],
["No virtuosity.","Nothing that only shows off skill."],
["Playful surface, serious structure.","Joke on top, rigour underneath."],
["One notch stranger.","Raise the weirdness one step above comfortable."],
["Hide the difficulty.","Complex inside, effortless outside."],
["Something from childhood.","Include one element from when you were small."],
["Look normal.","At first glance it must seem completely ordinary."],
["Annotate it.","Add a guide with precise markers: at 1'30\", top left, line 4."],
["For one picture.","It must accompany a specific image."],
["Make it obvious.","What would be confusing elsewhere must feel evident and joyful."]]};

